    <h2>About the workshop</h2>
    <p>Your breath is the one part of your nervous system you can steer on purpose. This introduction explains what pranayama is and why paying attention to how you breathe can influence how you feel, in body, mind and emotions.</p>
    <p>Together we look at how breath, nervous system and state of mind are linked, then try a handful of simple techniques you can use in a normal day: to calm down, reset, wake up and lift your energy, sharpen focus or simply arrive in the present moment.</p>
    <p>Beginners are very welcome. You do not need any earlier Yoga or breathwork experience.</p>

    <h2>During the session, you will</h2>
    <ul class="ce-list">
      <li>Find out what pranayama means and why awareness of the breath is such a useful everyday tool</li>
      <li>Discover breathwork as a powerful medicine</li>
      <li>Notice how different breathing patterns change the way your mind and body feel</li>
      <li>Practice simple and accessible pranayama techniques</li>
      <li>Experience a guided breathing practice</li>
      <li>Take away practical techniques for your daily routine or your working day</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Come as you are. Curiosity and your breath are all you need to bring.</p>

    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <p>Anybody interested to know more about pranayama.</p>

    <h2>Your facilitator</h2>
    <div class="ce-people">
      <div class="ce-person">
        <img class="ce-avatar" src="/images/ania-zielinska.webp?v=1" alt="Ania Zielińska, yoga teacher" width="104" height="104" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/>
        <div class="ce-person-body">
          <span class="role">Yoga Teacher · Holistic Health Coach · Life Realignment Mentor</span>
          <h4>Ania Zielińska</h4>
          <p>Ania Zielińska (Sunrise) works as a Yoga Teacher, Holistic Health Coach and Life Realignment Mentor, and has spent more than ten years in Yoga, meditation and holistic wellbeing. She has completed over 700 hours of yoga teacher training; alongside pranayama and meditation she teaches Hatha, Vinyasa and Yin Yoga.</p>
          <p>Her work goes beyond the physical practice of Yoga. As a Life Realignment Mentor, Ania supports people in creating meaningful changes across different areas of life — from wellbeing and weight loss, habits and mindset to self-awareness, relationships and personal growth. She pairs traditional Yogic practice with down-to-earth tools for daily life, to help people build awareness, calm, focus, energy and a closer connection with themselves.</p>
          <p>Yoga first came to Ania as a deep personal transformation, and it has become her passion to guide others Back to Themselves through movement, breath and mindfulness. She has taught Yoga around the world, in person and online, to people of many backgrounds and levels of experience.</p>
          <p>In her view, breath is among the simplest and strongest resources we have for shaping how we feel, respond and move through the day.</p>
